  "youtube": {
    "title": "Why \"This Week\" Never Comes #shorts",
    "description": "\"I'll work out this week\" has no day, no time and no place, so it never happens.\n\nIn a study with 248 students, those who wrote down exactly when and where they'd exercise (\"Monday, 7 AM, the park\") were far more likely to actually do it: 91% exercised, versus 38% of students who didn't make a plan. Psychologists call it an implementation intention, or an if-then plan.\n\nPick one goal and write one sentence: day, time, place.\n\nResearch: Milne, Orbell & Sheeran (2002), British Journal of Health Psychology.\n\n#shorts #discipline #habits #psychology #motivation #animation #selfimprovement",
